  "worked_solution": "Let's consider the situations in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. The events $F$ and $L$ are dependent because the first bottle is not replaced after Jack drank it. So, the number of lemon-lime flavored bottles is influenced by the result of the first choice, which then influences the result of the second choice.\n\n- Statement III is true. The events ${O}_{1}$ and ${O}_{2}$ are independent because the result of the first choice does not influence the second choice.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
